.\n\nSketch proof\n\nThe worst case is that G has two leaves {l}_{1} and {l}_{2}. In this situation, D can play the vertex adjacent to {l}_{1} in the first move to decrease \\pi by 50. If {l}_{2} is not red before Dominator’s next move, its unique neighbour cannot be red either, so playing it decreases \\pi by at least 27. Therefore, we have \\pi \\left(0\\right)-\\pi \\left(4\\right)\\ge 117. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTriangle decompositions of PG(n,2) (https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.19157)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Krotov ... A triangle design is balanced if all nonzero vectors are involved in the same number of triangles. Over the binary field GF$(2)$, we construct balanced triangle designs for all admissible $n$ (congruent to $1$ modulo $6$) and an infinite class of balanced block-divisible triangle designs.\nTitle: Triangle decompositions of PG(n,2)\nAuthors: Minjia Shi, Xiaoxiao Li, Denis S. Krotov\nDate: Sat Jul 27 03:40:36 2024\n\nWe define a triangle design as a partition of the set of $2$-dimensional subspaces of an $n$-dimensional vector space into triangles, where a triangle consists of three subspaces with the trivial, $0$-dimensional, intersection and $1$-dimensional mutual intersections. A triangle design is balanced if all nonzero vectors are involved in the same number of triangles. Over the binary field GF$(2)$, we construct balanced triangle designs for all admissible $n$ (congruent to $1$ modulo $6$) and an infinite class of balanced block-divisible triangle designs. We also prove that the existence of a triangle design over GF$(2)$ invariant under the action of the Singer cycle group is equivalent to the existence of a partition of $Z_{2^n-1}\\backslash\\{0\\}$ into special $18$-subsets and find such designs for $n=7$, $13$, $19$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTriangle decompositions of PG(n-1,2) - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/2407.19157v2)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; DOI: 10.1016/j.disc.2025.114664 ... A triangle design is balanced if all points are involved in the same number of triangles. We construct balanced triangle designs in PG$(n-1,2)$ for all admissible $n$ (congruent to $1$ modulo $6$) and an infinite class of balanced block-divisible triangle designs.\n\n## Triangle decompositions of PG(n-1,2)\n\nMinjia Shi, Xiaoxiao Li, Denis S. Krotov\n\nPublished: 2024-07-27 | Updated: 2025-07-08\n\nComments: v.2: final, revised, the terminology is partially changed to projective spaces, Heffter's difference problem is mentioned\n\nNote:\n\nJournal: Discrete Math. 349(1) 2026, 114664(1-13)\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.disc.2025.114664\n\ngraph group projective space partition\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe define a triangle design as a partition of the set of lines of a projective space into triangles, where a triangle consists of three pairwise intersecting lines with no common point. A triangle design is balanced if all points are involved in the same number of triangles. We construct balanced triangle designs in PG$(n-1,2)$ for all admissible $n$ (congruent to $1$ modulo $6$) and an infinite class of balanced block-divisible triangle designs. We also prove that the existence of a triangle design in PG$(n-1,2)$ invariant under the action of the Singer cycle group is equivalent to the existence of a partition of $Z_{2^n-1}\\backslash\\{0\\}$ into special $18$-subsets and find such partitions for $n=7$, $13$, $19$. Keywords: Subspace design, graph decomposition, triangle design, Heffter's difference problem.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExtremal Problems for Game Domination Number | SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics (https://doi.org/10.1137%2F120884742)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.9 years ago; Craw